---
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'FAQ — Imprint MCP Memory Layer';
const description =
  'What is an MCP memory layer? How is Imprint different from built-in IDE memory? Does my code leave my machine? Common questions answered.';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is an MCP memory layer?',
    a: 'MCP (Model Context Protocol) is the open standard Anthropic, OpenAI, and others use to expose tools to coding agents. An MCP memory layer is a server that speaks MCP and stores prior context — code chunks, decisions, bug fixes, architectural notes — so the agent can recall it instead of re-reading the whole repo every session. Imprint is a local-first implementation: vectors in Qdrant, facts in SQLite, embeddings via on-device ONNX.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is this different from Cursor or ChatGPT built-in memory?',
    a: 'Built-in memories are provider-bound, shallow, and cross-session at best. Imprint is agent-agnostic, indexed per-project, semantically searchable, and structured (tags for language, layer, domain, topic). One memory store is shared across Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Codex CLI, and Cline — whatever you use today and whatever you switch to next.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does my code ever leave my machine?',
    a: 'Not by default. The Qdrant daemon runs on 127.0.0.1:6333. Embeddings come from Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B via ONNX Runtime — no network call. The knowledge graph is local SQLite. Two things send data out, and only when you ask: `imprint sync` streams the workspace you choose through a relay, end-to-end encrypted with the session’s share code so the relay sees only ciphertext, and opt-in LLM topic tagging (`imprint config set tagger.llm true`) calls the provider you pick (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, or local Ollama / vLLM).',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why not just wait for bigger context windows?',
    a: 'Bigger contexts still pay for every token at inference, still forget between sessions, and still degrade on long conversations. Imprint flips the problem: the context window stays tight, the agent pulls only the 5–10 chunks relevant to the current question. Our benchmark shows Claude Code dropping from 10.3M total tokens to 3.0M across the same 150-run suite — the agent simply did not need the rest.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which agents does it work with?',
    a: 'Any MCP-capable host. `imprint setup all` auto-wires Claude Code (with hard enforcement via a PreToolUse hook), Claude Desktop, Cursor, GitHub Copilot (VS Code agent mode), Codex CLI, Cline and OpenClaw. Adding a new host is a config file and a CLI subcommand away.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I share memory across my machines or with my team?',
    a: 'Yes. `imprint sync serve` prints a one-time share code; the other machine joins with `imprint sync <code>`, the serving side approves its device, and memories and facts arrive deduplicated. Joining only receives: add `--two-way` to send back as well, and you are shown the serving device and asked before anything leaves. The serving side can be `--send-only` or `--receive-only`. Sessions are end-to-end encrypted: the code becomes the key (SPAKE2) without crossing the relay, so even the default public relay cannot read your memories. Project identity comes from the manifest (package.json, go.mod, pyproject.toml…), so the same repo lines up on every machine. Sync is on demand, not a live shared database.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I share only part of my memory?',
    a: 'Yes, through workspaces. Each workspace is a separate memory with its own vector collection and fact graph. Copy a project, topic or single source into a dedicated workspace with `imprint migrate --from default --to team --project <name> --copy`, then sync just that one with `imprint sync serve --workspace team --send-only`. Your own workspace keeps everything, and nothing else is sent. The dashboard has the same controls.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it slow my agent down?',
    a: 'Search itself is tens of milliseconds against a local Qdrant. Net turn count can go up slightly (search → answer takes one extra call), but each turn carries a tiny fraction of the tokens. Across the benchmark, duration drops in parallel with cost on debug and cross-project questions, stays flat on creation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can it index JS-heavy docs sites or complex documents?',
    a: 'Yes, via two opt-in extractors. For JS-rendered pages, install the obscura headless browser (Apache 2.0) and set `imprint config set ingest.use_obscura true` — `imprint ingest-url` will pipe every URL through a real browser before extraction. For richer document support (archives, Apple iWork, ODF, email/mbox, image OCR), install kreuzberg (`pip install kreuzberg[all]`) and set `ingest.use_kreuzberg true`. kreuzberg is under the Elastic License 2.0 — internal and self-hosted use is fine; SaaS re-hosting of its extraction is not.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does uninstalling look like?',
    a: '`imprint disable` tears down every MCP entry from every host config it previously wrote, stops the Qdrant daemon, and preserves `data/` and `.venv/` so `imprint enable` brings everything back instantly. Full removal is `imprint uninstall`, which also deletes the venv and data; add `--keep-data` to keep your memories.',
  },
];
---

<Landing title={title} description={description} pathname="/faq/">
  <Nav />
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-ink">← Back to overview</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">FAQ</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[color:var(--color-text-muted)]">
      Short answers to what developers usually ask before installing Imprint. Longer explanations live in the <a class="underline hover:text-ink" href="/architecture">architecture</a> and <a class="underline hover:text-ink" href="/mcp">MCP tools</a> docs.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="group rounded-xl bg-[color:var(--color-surface)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] open:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/60 transition">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="font-semibold">{item.q}</span>
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text-muted)] group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-[color:var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            {item.a.split('`').map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? <code class="cmd">{part}</code> : part))}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      set:html={JSON.stringify({
        '@context': 'https://schema.org',
        '@type': 'FAQPage',
        mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
          '@type': 'Question',
          name: f.q,
          acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a.replaceAll('`', '') },
        })),
      })}
    />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Landing>
